    'about.philo.04.p':'Designing dynamic landscapes, anchored in their context, respectful of ecological balances and open to the evolution of the living world. Ecology is not a constraint — it is the condition of permanence.',
    'about.philo.05.h4':'Architecture as partner',
    'about.philo.05.p':'The best gardens I have worked on began with a conversation with the architect. When landscape and architecture speak the same language, the result feels whole rather than assembled.',
    'about.philo.06.h4':'From sketch to completion — and beyond',
    'about.philo.06.p':'Complete support, from design through site supervision, in constant dialogue. Once the garden is delivered, the relationship continues — maintenance, evolution, and the long life of the project.',
    'about.role.label.1':'The clients','about.role.h2.1':'A genuinely<br>shared project.',
    'about.role.p1.1':'A relationship of trust with clients is essential: it allows a genuinely shared project to be built, founded on their expectations and enriched by my expertise. I support every stage, from design to site supervision, in constant dialogue to guarantee a precise, accomplished result.',
